### Ambulance Protocols API — REST Client Test File
### Compatible with: VS Code REST Client extension, JetBrains HTTP Client, IntelliJ IDEA
### Usage: Click "Send Request" above any request block
###
### Prerequisites:
###   1. OPENAI_API_KEY set in .env (must start with sk-)
###   2. Server running: uvicorn api.main:app --reload --port 8000
###   3. Confirm warm: GET /health → agent_ready: true
###
### API schema reference:
###   patientInfo.ageGroup : "infant" | "child" | "adolescent" | "adult" | "elderly"
###   incidentInfo.priority: "P1" | "P2" | "P3" | "P4"
###   incidentInfo.consciousness: "alert" | "verbal" | "pain" | "unconscious"
###   incidentInfo.breathing : "normal" | "laboured" | "absent"

@base_url     = http://127.0.0.1:8000
@content_type = application/json


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 1 — SYSTEM ENDPOINTS
# =============================================================================

### 1.1 Health check — confirms agent is initialised and model name is correct
GET {{base_url}}/health
Accept: application/json


### 1.2 OpenAPI docs (paste URL into browser)
# GET {{base_url}}/docs


# =============================================================================
# SECTION 2 — P1 IMMEDIATELY LIFE-THREATENING
# =============================================================================

### 2.1 Cardiac arrest — highest-priority anchor
# Expected: protocol for CPR, AED, airway management, rapid transport
POST {{base_url}}/em_protocols_rag
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

{
  "dispatchId": "DISP-001",
  "patientInfo": {
    "ageGroup": "adult",
    "approxAge": "58",
    "sex": "male"
  },
  "incidentInfo": {
    "description": "65-year-old male collapsed, not breathing, no pulse, bystander performing CPR",
    "priority": "P1",
    "consciousness": "unconscious",
    "breathing": "absent",
    "activelyBleeding": false,
    "medicalHistory": "hypertension"
  }
}


### 2.2 Gunshot wound — penetrating abdominal trauma
# Expected: haemorrhage control, IV access, rapid transport protocol
POST {{base_url}}/em_protocols_rag
Content-Type: {{content_type}}

